                <pb facs="0788" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.635 Neep/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-05T00:00:00-00:44">March 5,
                        1938—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received March 6—8:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Referring to your 9, March 3, 5 p.m., I am informed by President Barclay that
                    he conferred with Caffe yesterday and that he has <pb facs="0789" n="781"
                        xml:id="pg781"/> cabled his Minister at Paris as outlined in penultimate
                    paragraph of my 14, February 21, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
